  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3205.07 Certificate of Appointment Not Transferred.\n\n(a) Each certificate of appointment shall be limited to the person in whose name and place of business it has been issued.\n\n(b) A certificate of appointment shall not be transferred to any other person, business or location and shall not be altered or modified in any manner.\n\n(c) A certificate of appointment shall be presented to any individual authorized by the department upon demand or surrendered to the department, if required, after a hearing.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07; amd by #9184, eff 6-20-08; paras. (a) & (b) EXPIRED: 6-22-15; ss by #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
